  "body": "## What changed\n\n2D Contour tabs now leave a bridge of the tab width that the user sets.\n\n- `ring::tab_window` (new): the tab window on the tool-centre ring is `tab_width + tool_diameter`. Before, it was `tab_width` alone. The cutter disc removes `D/2` more material past each window end, so the bridge on the channel centre line was `tab_width - D`. A tab width of `D` or less left no bridge, and the part came free with no message.\n- `ring::tabs_fill_note` (new): when the tab windows fill the whole loop, the tabbed level cuts nothing. The operation notes now say this. Before, this was silent.\n- `contour.rs` calls the two helpers (3 lines more in a file that was over the 400-line target before this PR).\n\n## Readings\n\n- Square 40 x 40, 6 mm cutter, outside contour, bottom level tabbed:\n  - 4 tabs of 6 mm: four bridges of 6.0 mm (before: none).\n  - 4 tabs of 5 mm: four bridges of 5.0 mm (before: none, the cuts overlapped by 1 mm).\n  - 3 tabs of 10 mm: three bridges of 10.0 mm (before: 4 mm).\n- `tabs_hold_the_part_until_the_floor`: the tabbed level is `4 x (6 + 10) = 64` mm shorter than the full ring (measured 64.0017 mm; the 1.7 um comes from window ends that fall on corner arcs).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/contour_tabs.rs` (new): measures each bridge as the swept disc of the posted feeds against points on the tool-centre ring. Five tests, including the fill note.\n- `crates/motion/tests/machining2d.rs`:\n  - `tabs_hold_the_part_until_the_floor`: new length.\n  - `contour_tabs_stand_down_the_entry_arms` and `contour_hop_rides_the_tall_tab_top`: these used four 6 mm tabs with a 10 mm tool on a 40 mm centre ring. No tab can stand there. They now use two 4 mm tabs; their asserts did not change.\n- `crates/app/tests/first_router_part.rs`: `examples/first-router-part.camproj` regenerated with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`. Its contour now has 14 mm gaps on the centre path for the 8 mm tabs with the 6 mm cutter. The write also took the project file from version 62 to 67 and added the drill's break-through note.\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` on the final code: 22 steps, 0 failed (motion lib and the touched motion suites, app `arc_entry`, `solid_law_goldens`, `wall_arc_entry`). Then `first_router_part`: 4 passed after the regenerate. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No air cut on a machine.\n- Control compensation (G41/G42) rings use the same window; on a straight wall the bridge is the same. Not measured separately.\n- Wire EDM tabs (`wire_edm/tabs.rs`) are a different law and are not changed.\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/2480-tab-bridge-width.md`.\n\nChangelog: 2D Contour: the tab width is now the width of the bridge that stays on the part (the tab window on the tool path is the tab width plus the tool diameter). Before, a tab width equal to or less than the tool diameter left no tab, and the part came free.\n\nFixes #2480\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
